Z||000009||Fiero5||10-29-2001||08:29 PM||||I saw this advertised on the Fiero list a few weeks ago:<P>"Sat, 20 Oct 2001 11:26:24 -0400<P>From: "grinthock" &lt;grinthock@softhome.net&gt;<BR>To: fiero-list@fiero.org<BR>Date: Sat, 20 Oct 2001 11:22:14 -0400<BR>X-Priority: 3 (Normal)<BR>Importance: Normal<BR>Subject: (Fiero) NEW Forum<BR>Resent-From: fiero-list@fiero.org<BR>X-Mailing-List: &lt;fiero-list@fiero.org&gt; archive/latest/109104<BR>X-Loop: fiero-list@fiero.org<BR>Resent-Sender: fiero-list-request@fiero.org<BR>Status:   <P>I have put up a new forum at <A HREF="http://www.fieroworld.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroworld.com</A>  click on the forum link.<BR>It's going to be for all types of vehicles but there is a fiero section, any<BR>ideas on forums/topics/sections email me directly.<P>Thanks<P><BR>-- <BR>All messages to the Fiero-list must be strictly Fiero-related." <P><BR>Isn't this Grinthock dude the one that was upset at Cliff not too long ago about his banner and it being "castrated"?<P>I think that for a forum to work, it needs a bunch of members doesn't it?<P>Just a thought.<P>Steve||||reg||9
